Falsifies `memory_region_heap::verification::a_grow_at_the_cap_is_a_refusal`.

The defect: a run is a success when it maps at least what the request needed, with no requirement
that it mapped anything. At the cap a request of no bytes needs no page, the run maps none, and
`grow` answers true, so `alloc` retries a question whose answer cannot change. This is the form
the function had before milestone 1100 item 6.

Expected to fail: `assert!(!run_succeeded(got, need_pages))` for a run of no pages against a
request of none. Red in under a second on 2026-11-15.

diff --git a/crates/memory_region_heap/src/lib.rs b/crates/memory_region_heap/src/lib.rs
index b961c1948..09fc25ba4 100644
--- a/crates/memory_region_heap/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/memory_region_heap/src/lib.rs
@@ -486,7 +486,7 @@ fn growth_pages(committed: u64, maximum: u64, need: u64) -> Option<(u64, u64)> {
 /// needed none: the caller retries after a `true`, and a retry after nothing changed would ask the
 /// same question forever.
 fn run_succeeded(got_pages: u64, need_pages: u64) -> bool {
-    got_pages > 0 && got_pages >= need_pages
+    got_pages >= need_pages
 }
 
